# term in a test build: COM2 carries the kernel's log, so there is no
# terminal. A release build makes COM2 the modem's line.
program: shell
keys: term\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>term
COM2 carries the kernel's log in this build; a release build
makes it the modem's line.
A:\>
